    "readmeMarkdown": "## SQLite (community / archived reference server)\n\nRuns the official **`mcp-server-sqlite`** reference server over stdio via `uvx`, pinned to `==2025.4.25`. This server lives in the **archived** [`modelcontextprotocol/servers-archived`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers-archived/tree/main/src/sqlite) repository \u2014 it is a community/archived reference server, so the version is pinned and future releases are not auto-pulled without a re-vet. No connection string, password, or secret is required: the server opens **`${WORKSPACE}/pupu-mcp.sqlite`**, a local SQLite database file inside the selected agent workspace.\n\n### Use a disposable, non-production workspace\n\nThe agent can read **every table and row** in this database file \u2014 reading the database **is** data exfiltration. Use a **disposable / non-production** workspace whose `pupu-mcp.sqlite` file you are comfortable exposing in full; never copy production or sensitive data into it.\n\n### Gated vs. ungated tools\n\nThe read tools \u2014 `read_query` (SELECT only), `list_tables`, and `describe_table` \u2014 run without a prompt. Every tool that **mutates state** is gated behind explicit confirmation:\n\n- `write_query` \u2014 INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE.\n- `create_table` \u2014 CREATE TABLE (DDL).\n- `append_insight` \u2014 writes to the server's `memo://insights` resource.\n\nEven with writes gated, treat the connected database as fully readable by the agent."
